{{Bug|Estormo's low agression will cause him to accept a yield. He may also flee combat and is no longer hostile after regaining enough health.|confirmed=1}}
{{Bug|Sometimes, the after-images of Savos and his companions will not engage in their intended dialogue, and stand still instead.|confirmed=1}}
{{Bug|One or more of the ghosts of Savos and his companions may be missing from their intended scenes.|confirmed=1}}
{{Bug|Morokei may not attack at all, simply floating towards you and not doing anything.|confirmed=1}}
**{{Pc22}} Use the <code>prid 00086CF4</code> then <code>kill</code> [[Skyrim:Console|console commands]] to kill Morokei; the quest will advance directly to "Find the staff of Magnus".
{{Bug|After killing the skeletal dragon, it will sometimes reanimate.}}
{{Bug|The quest may fail to start after completing [[Skyrim:Containment|Containment]], and even trying manually start or end it with the console will not work.|confirmed=1}}
** Try completing any quest related to Labyrinthian before starting Containment mission, for some unknown reasons the quest fails to start if there is another quest with marker pointing to Labyrinthian.
**{{Pc22}} Make sure that all of the NPCs in the College of Winterhold are still present and enabled; For example, you may not be able to find [[Skyrim:Arniel Gane|Arniel]] because he is disabled. In order to solve this issue, simply open the console and type <code>prid <RefID></code> then <code>enable</code> to re-enable a specific NPC.
{{Bug|The loading screens for Labyrinthian were meant to stop once this quest is finished, but they never stop due to incorrect conditions governing this.|USKP|2.0.1}}
{{Bug|This quest may fail to start if either [[Skyrim:Arniel Gane|Arniel Gane]] or [[Skyrim:Faralda|Faralda]] are unavailable (killed, disabled, etc). Their parts in this quest are optional so their aliases have been marked to indicate this. The same issue can also prevent [[Skyrim:The Eye of Magnus|The Eye of Magnus]] from starting as well.|USSEP|4.2.6}}
{{Bug|If you leave Labyrinthian early on and then come back, Morokei will sometimes not talk to you at all as you advance through the dungeon, but the magicka drain effect will still happen.}}

